# Human review is the floor, not the default (ADR-0028, amending ADR-0017). Only the paths
# that could weaken the security posture or the merge gate itself wait for a person.
# Taste-bearing paths (typeset, theme, contracts, ADRs) go through the taste-review queue instead.

# Security posture (ADR-0009): the sanitiser, the CSP and the shell's capabilities.
/packages/core/src/sanitize/            @inkstrata
/apps/desktop/src-tauri/tauri.conf.json @inkstrata
/apps/desktop/src-tauri/capabilities/   @inkstrata

# The gate itself: CI, release, this file, and the code that decides a merge.
/.github/                               @inkstrata
/orchestration/approve.mjs              @inkstrata
/orchestration/merge-bar.mjs            @inkstrata
/orchestration/cycle.mjs                @inkstrata
